From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:59:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mixBus_internal: clear unwritten scratch before panning a
 voice

When a voice's fixed-point step is zero (relative speed near zero, or a
step beyond the fixed-point range that is forced to zero), the resample
loop never runs, but panAndExpand still read aScratch, which held the
previous voice's resampled data. Zero any part of the scratch the loop
did not write.

Found while auditing upstream #343 (infinite loop when writesamples is
0); that loop could not be reproduced from the current code, but the
same zero-progress case played stale audio.
---
 src/core/soloud.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud.cpp b/src/core/soloud.cpp
index d53ab70..6a10aad 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud.cpp
@@ -1789,6 +1789,17 @@ namespace SoLoud
 					// Move source pointer onwards (writesamples may be zero)
 					voice->mSrcOffset += writesamples * step_fixed;
 				}
+
+				// A zero step (speed near zero, or above the fixed-point range) skips
+				// the resampler; don't pan another voice's scratch data into the mix.
+				if (outofs < aSamplesToRead)
+				{
+					unsigned int k;
+					for (k = 0; k < voice->mChannels; k++)
+					{
+						memset(aScratch + k * aBufferSize + outofs, 0, sizeof(float) * (aSamplesToRead - outofs));
+					}
+				}
 				
 				// Handle panning and channel expansion (and/or shrinking)
 				panAndExpand(voice, aBuffer, aSamplesToRead, aBufferSize, aScratch, aChannels);
